  "question": {
    "text": "The graph of an object's motion (along the $x-$ axis) is shown in the figure. The instantaneous velocity of the object at points $A$ and $B$ are $v_A$ and $v_B$ respectively. Then\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/i3CuCjh06QLGOPMuy80QNql3joQDbDPzpt8cK1tGfOM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mMSn9",
      "text": "\n$v_A=v_B=0.5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "0KHgN",
      "text": "\n$v_A=0.5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s} < v_B$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "QiEgM",
      "text": "\n$v_A=0.5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}>v_B$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lBkYZ",
      "text": "\n$v_A=v_B=2 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Instantaneous velocity $v=\\frac{\\Delta x}{\\Delta t}$ From graph, $v_A=\\frac{\\Delta x_A}{\\Delta t_A}=\\frac{4 m}{8 s}=0.5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ and $v_B=\\frac{\\Delta x_B}{\\Delta t_B}=\\frac{8 m}{16 s}=0.5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ i.e., $v_A=v_B=0.5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
    "image": null
  },
